      "title": "Implement CSV parser and row-to-object mapping",
      "status": "running",
      "plan": "Implement parseCsv(text) and toObjects(rows) in src/csv.js. parseCsv is a character scanner handling quoted fields that contain commas, line breaks and doubled quotes for a literal quote, with LF and CRLF line endings, no phantom row for a trailing final line break, and [] for empty text. toObjects takes the first row as header, returns one object per remaining row, and pads short rows with empty strings. Add tests in test/csv.test.js run via node --test through the package test script. Acceptance: the test suite passes and behaviour matches every bullet in the request.",
